<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>
	<!--
		Missing body part penalty - settings section. These rows feed the C# half
		(CarryCapacityMissingParts.dll in Common/Assemblies); they do NOT patch any defs.
		The DLL reads the values once at startup via XmlExtensions.SettingsManager and only
		acts when the section's master checkbox (ToggleSectionMissingParts, created by
		CCFB_Section, default OFF) is ticked. Defaults here MUST stay in sync with the
		compiled defaults in MissingPartsBootstrap.cs. Values are NEGATIVE (they remove
		carry capacity); the C# uses the absolute value.
		Value design (June 2026, VitaKaninen's table): children of each limb sum EXACTLY to
		their parent (femur 15 + tibia 5 + foot 5 = leg 25%; clavicle 5 + arm 10 = shoulder 15%;
		humerus 2.5 + radius 2.5 + hand 5 = arm 10%; 5 fingers/toes = hand/foot 5%), so with
		default values the per-limb cap is a safety net, not a daily occurrence.
		Spine and Pelvis share ONE row/key (MissingPartSpinePelvis): each needs the other to
		work, so the penalty applies if either is gone and is not doubled if both are.
		Row args for CCFB_PartRow: key | label | toggle default | kg default | section tag | tooltip.
	-->
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.ApplyPatch">
		<patchName>CCFB_Section</patchName>
		<arguments>
			<li>Missing body parts</li>
			<li>MissingParts</li>
			<li>false</li>
		</arguments>
	</Operation>

	<!-- Explainer text at the top of the section body (inserted BEFORE the SplitColumn),
	     then the floor row as the first actual setting. Guarded on the floor key. -->
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.Conditional">
		<xpath>Defs/XmlExtensions.SettingsMenuDef[modId="Vita.CarryCapacityFromBionics"]/settings//li[key="MissingPartFloor"]</xpath>
		<caseFalse>
			<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.PatchOperationInsert">
				<xpath>Defs/XmlExtensions.SettingsMenuDef[modId="Vita.CarryCapacityFromBionics"]/settings//li[tag="CCFB_MissingParts"]</xpath>
				<value>
					<li Class="XmlExtensions.Setting.Text">
						<text>Each enabled part below subtracts its value from a pawn's mass carry capacity (inventory and caravan weight) while that part is missing; damaged parts subtract in proportion to lost HP. Bionics, prosthetics and other replacements count as present. A safety net keeps the math sane: only the topmost missing part is counted, and a limb's combined penalties can never exceed the value of its topmost part - losing pieces of a limb never costs more than losing the whole limb. Penalties never reduce a pawn below the minimum set here. Hover any row for details.</text>
					</li>
					<li Class="XmlExtensions.Setting.Gap">
						<spacing>12</spacing>
					</li>
				</value>
			</Operation>
			<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.PatchOperationAdd">
				<xpath>Defs/XmlExtensions.SettingsMenuDef[modId="Vita.CarryCapacityFromBionics"]/settings//li[tag="CCFB_MissingParts"]/leftCol</xpath>
				<value>
					<li Class="XmlExtensions.Setting.Text">
						<text>Minimum carry capacity</text>
						<tooltip>Combined penalties never reduce a pawn below this many kg. At 0, a badly mangled pawn can carry nothing in inventory but still wears gear, wields weapons and eats normally. Raise it (e.g. 10) if you do not want crippled pawns to weigh down caravans.</tooltip>
					</li>
				</value>
			</Operation>
			<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.PatchOperationAdd">
				<xpath>Defs/XmlExtensions.SettingsMenuDef[modId="Vita.CarryCapacityFromBionics"]/settings//li[tag="CCFB_MissingParts"]/rightCol</xpath>
				<value>
					<li Class="XmlExtensions.Setting.Numeric">
						<decimals>2</decimals>
						<padLeft>85</padLeft>
						<key>MissingPartFloor</key>
						<label>Minimum in kg</label>
						<defaultValue>0</defaultValue>
					</li>
				</value>
			</Operation>
			<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.PatchOperationAdd">
				<xpath>Defs/XmlExtensions.SettingsMenuDef[modId="Vita.CarryCapacityFromBionics"]/settings//li[@Class="XmlExtensions.Setting.Button"][key="ToggleSectionMissingParts"]/actions/li/keys</xpath>
				<value>
					<li>MissingPartFloor</li>
				</value>
			</Operation>
		</caseFalse>
	</Operation>

	<!-- Per-part rows, in body-tree order (spine/pelvis, then leg subtree, then arm subtree) -->
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.ApplyPatch">
		<patchName>CCFB_PartRow</patchName>
		<arguments>
			<li>MissingPartSpinePelvis</li>
			<li>Spine/Pelvis</li>
			<li>false</li>
			<li>-7</li>
			<li>MissingParts</li>
			<li>One penalty for the pair: it applies while the spine or the pelvis is missing or damaged, and is not doubled if both are gone. A pawn missing either cannot walk, but the value still cuts their inventory space and their share of a caravan's weight pool.</li>
		</arguments>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.ApplyPatch">
		<patchName>CCFB_PartRow</patchName>
		<arguments>
			<li>MissingPartLeg</li>
			<li>Leg (each)</li>
			<li>false</li>
			<li>-8.75</li>
			<li>MissingParts</li>
			<li>Top of the leg. Caps the whole leg: femur, tibia, foot and toes together can never subtract more than this value.</li>
		</arguments>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.ApplyPatch">
		<patchName>CCFB_PartRow</patchName>
		<arguments>
			<li>MissingPartFemur</li>
			<li>Femur (each)</li>
			<li>false</li>
			<li>-5.25</li>
			<li>MissingParts</li>
			<li>Inner thigh bone - can be destroyed while the leg itself survives.</li>
		</arguments>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.ApplyPatch">
		<patchName>CCFB_PartRow</patchName>
		<arguments>
			<li>MissingPartTibia</li>
			<li>Tibia (each)</li>
			<li>false</li>
			<li>-1.75</li>
			<li>MissingParts</li>
			<li>Inner shin bone - can be destroyed while the leg itself survives.</li>
		</arguments>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.ApplyPatch">
		<patchName>CCFB_PartRow</patchName>
		<arguments>
			<li>MissingPartFoot</li>
			<li>Foot (each)</li>
			<li>false</li>
			<li>-1.75</li>
			<li>MissingParts</li>
			<li>If the whole leg is gone, only the leg value applies - the foot is not charged again.</li>
		</arguments>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.ApplyPatch">
		<patchName>CCFB_PartRow</patchName>
		<arguments>
			<li>MissingPartToe</li>
			<li>Toe (each)</li>
			<li>false</li>
			<li>-0.35</li>
			<li>MissingParts</li>
			<li>Per missing toe (5 per foot).</li>
		</arguments>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.ApplyPatch">
		<patchName>CCFB_PartRow</patchName>
		<arguments>
			<li>MissingPartShoulder</li>
			<li>Shoulder (each)</li>
			<li>false</li>
			<li>-5.25</li>
			<li>MissingParts</li>
			<li>Top of the arm. Caps the whole arm: clavicle, arm, bones, hand and fingers together can never subtract more than this value. Bionic and prosthetic arms install here - a replaced shoulder has no penalty.</li>
		</arguments>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.ApplyPatch">
		<patchName>CCFB_PartRow</patchName>
		<arguments>
			<li>MissingPartClavicle</li>
			<li>Clavicle (each)</li>
			<li>false</li>
			<li>-1.75</li>
			<li>MissingParts</li>
			<li>Collarbone - can be destroyed while the shoulder itself survives.</li>
		</arguments>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.ApplyPatch">
		<patchName>CCFB_PartRow</patchName>
		<arguments>
			<li>MissingPartArm</li>
			<li>Arm (each)</li>
			<li>false</li>
			<li>-3.5</li>
			<li>MissingParts</li>
			<li>Arm severed below the shoulder.</li>
		</arguments>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.ApplyPatch">
		<patchName>CCFB_PartRow</patchName>
		<arguments>
			<li>MissingPartHumerus</li>
			<li>Humerus (each)</li>
			<li>false</li>
			<li>-0.875</li>
			<li>MissingParts</li>
			<li>Inner upper-arm bone - can be destroyed while the arm itself survives.</li>
		</arguments>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.ApplyPatch">
		<patchName>CCFB_PartRow</patchName>
		<arguments>
			<li>MissingPartRadius</li>
			<li>Radius (each)</li>
			<li>false</li>
			<li>-0.875</li>
			<li>MissingParts</li>
			<li>Inner forearm bone - can be destroyed while the arm itself survives.</li>
		</arguments>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.ApplyPatch">
		<patchName>CCFB_PartRow</patchName>
		<arguments>
			<li>MissingPartHand</li>
			<li>Hand (each)</li>
			<li>false</li>
			<li>-1.75</li>
			<li>MissingParts</li>
			<li>If the whole arm is gone, only the arm or shoulder value applies - the hand is not charged again.</li>
		</arguments>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.ApplyPatch">
		<patchName>CCFB_PartRow</patchName>
		<arguments>
			<li>MissingPartFinger</li>
			<li>Finger (each)</li>
			<li>false</li>
			<li>-0.35</li>
			<li>MissingParts</li>
			<li>Per missing finger (5 per hand).</li>
		</arguments>
	</Operation>
</Patch>
